okf_version: "1.0"
knowledge:
  task:
    id: codex-external-provider-mcp-tool-search-research-20260826
    date: "2026-08-26"
    mode: research_only
    objective: >-
      Determine whether missing direct MCP tools in a Ciel-routed Codex
      session are limited to GPT-5.x versus one provider/model, and distinguish
      Mia's local workaround from Ciel Runtime and Codex behavior.

  constraints:
    functional_code_modified: false
    runtime_configuration_modified: false
    remote_configuration_modified: false
    deployment_performed: false

  mia_local_workaround:
    files:
      - path: /home/mia/.ai-net/mcp-call.mjs
        kind: new local JSON-RPC MCP client
        observed_mtime_utc: "2026-08-26 07:39:50.941046698"
      - path: /home/mia/.ai-net/readback.mjs
        kind: new local readback helper
    transcript_evidence: >-
      Mia created mcp-call.mjs with apply_patch after the active Codex tool list
      did not expose AI-Net tool calls, then used it to call the configured
      AI-Net MCP HTTP endpoint directly.
    scope_conclusion: >-
      Successful helper calls confirm the MCP server and credentials worked.
      They do not prove Codex exposed those MCP tools directly to the model.
      Neither helper modifies Ciel Runtime, Codex configuration, or AI-Net
      server code.

  corrected_codex_mechanism:
    codex_version: "0.149.1"
    official_source_commit: ff29a44391deccde0aba0f8390337d7f3c319ea4
    evidence:
      - >-
        codex-rs/core/src/tools/spec_plan.rs defines search_tool_enabled as
        model_info.supports_search_tool AND provider namespace_tools support.
      - >-
        The same file supplies search_tool_enabled to MCP registration and
        selects deferred exposure only when search is enabled; otherwise it
        removes deferred exposure and retains direct exposure.
      - >-
        codex-rs/models-manager/src/model_info.rs gives unknown-model fallback
        metadata supports_search_tool=false.
    contradiction: >-
      The earlier claim that the removed feature flag
      ToolSearchAlwaysDeferMcpTools directly controls this behavior is
      inconsistent with the official 0.149.1 source. The effective predicate
      is model metadata plus provider capability, not that removed flag.

  ciel_catalog_projection:
    source_evidence:
      - file: ciel_runtime_support/codex_model_catalog.py
        lines: "60-72, 87-114"
        observation: >-
          Ciel selects bundled gpt-5.2 as the template, deep-copies the entire
          model record, changes selected routing fields, and then applies only
          explicitly supplied metadata overrides.
      - file: ciel_runtime_support/codex_launch_configuration.py
        lines: "177-237"
        observation: >-
          Every non-native routed launch with an alias and context window gets
          a generated catalog. Native Codex launches skip this Ciel catalog.
      - file: ciel_runtime_support/providers/alibaba.py
        lines: "30-38, 248-258"
        observation: >-
          Qwen 3.8 supplies catalog overrides but does not override
          supports_search_tool, so the GPT-5.2 template value remains.
    confirmed_generated_catalogs_with_supports_search_tool_true:
      local:
        - deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-1m
        - deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash
        - alitoken/qwen3.8-max
        - ollama/qwen3
        - zai/glm-5.2
        - anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6
        - anthropic/claude-opus-5
        - kimi/k3-1m
      mia:
        - ollama/qwen3.8-27b
        - ollama-cloud/deepseek-v4-pro-0813
        - openrouter/stealth-ox-alpha
        - zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3-1m
        - zai-start-plan/glm-5.3-1m
        - zai/glm-5.3-1m

  scope_conclusion:
    confirmed: >-
      The capability projection is common to Ciel-routed non-native Codex
      models, not limited to Ollama Qwen or to one provider. The generated
      catalogs listed above all advertise supports_search_tool=true.
    excluded: >-
      Direct native Codex/OpenAI launches skip Ciel's generated model catalog.
    not_yet_proven: >-
      This research does not establish that every listed provider fails at
      runtime. Actual failure depends on whether that provider and Ciel's wire
      adapter implement the Codex tool-search request/response contract. Each
      provider requires an independent wire-level test before a failure claim.

  live_toggle_evaluation:
    stock_slash_command:
      observed: >-
        Codex 0.149.1 defines /mcp only for listing configured MCP tools, with
        the single optional argument verbose. It has no direct/deferred mode
        toggle.
    disk_catalog_change:
      restart_required: true
      evidence: >-
        Codex reads model_catalog_json while constructing Config, and a supplied
        catalog creates a StaticModelsManager whose model vector is copied at
        construction. Editing the JSON file does not mutate that manager.
    preloaded_dual_model_alias:
      restart_required_after_initial_launch: false
      evidence: >-
        TurnContext.with_model resolves fresh ModelInfo from the existing shared
        models manager. Therefore two aliases preloaded in the initial catalog,
        one supports_search_tool=false and one true, can be switched by the
        built-in /model command for subsequent turns.
      router_requirement: >-
        Both aliases must resolve to the same intended upstream provider model;
        this mapping does not exist in the current implementation and would
        require implementation and validation.
    custom_prompt_command_limit: >-
      A Ciel-installed prompt/slash asset is expanded into model input. It can
      change router-side state but cannot by itself replace the client-side
      ModelInfo already held by Codex, so it cannot provide a no-restart live
      MCP exposure toggle on the current single-alias design.

  automatic_capability_resolution:
    manual_model_database_required: false
    limitation: >-
      Generic OpenAI-compatible model discovery does not provide a portable
      supports_search_tool capability contract. Model names and ordinary
      function-call support are insufficient evidence of Tool Search support.
    state_model:
      values: [supported, unsupported, unknown]
      resolution_order:
        - Native authoritative model catalog metadata, when present.
        - Explicit provider/profile capability supplied from official provider evidence.
        - Cached result of an exact wire-level compatibility probe.
        - Unknown falls back to direct MCP exposure.
    probe_identity:
      - provider id
      - normalized upstream base URL or endpoint family
      - wire protocol
      - exact upstream model id
      - provider or model revision when available
      - probe contract version
    probe_contract: >-
      Send a minimal client-executed tool_search request. A protocol rejection
      is evidence of unsupported. A valid tool_search_call followed by accepted
      tool_search_output and a call to the loaded dummy function is evidence of
      supported. A successful text response that does not perform the requested
      search remains unknown rather than being classified unsupported.
    persistence: >-
      Store only automatically observed probe results with evidence, timestamp,
      and TTL. This is a compatibility cache for encountered targets, not a
      hand-maintained database of every model.
    official_basis: >-
      OpenAI Tool Search documentation defines tool_search, defer_loading,
      tool_search_call, and tool_search_output as a distinct multi-step
      protocol and states that only gpt-5.4 and later OpenAI models support it.

  kimi_k3_example:
    confirmed_official_contract: >-
      Moonshot's Kimi K3 repository documents OpenAI- and
      Anthropic-compatible APIs and ordinary tool_calls with preserved
      reasoning_content across turns.
    not_confirmed: >-
      The inspected official Kimi materials do not establish support for the
      distinct OpenAI Responses tool_search/tool_search_output protocol.
    first_connection_resolution:
      initial_state: unknown
      catalog_value: "supports_search_tool=false"
      mcp_exposure: direct
      effect: >-
        Codex receives the MCP tools directly as normal callable tool schemas;
        no Tool Search capability is claimed merely from the kimi-k3 model id.
    identity_warning: >-
      Moonshot OpenAI-compatible, Moonshot Anthropic-compatible, OpenRouter,
      and self-hosted vLLM routes for the same Kimi K3 weights are distinct
      compatibility targets. Probe/cache identity must include endpoint and
      wire protocol, not only the model name.
    upgrade_rule: >-
      Only an official provider capability declaration or a successful complete
      probe for that exact route may promote the cached state to supported.

  optimistic_true_fallback_evaluation:
    possible_for_hard_failures: true
    hard_failure_examples:
      - upstream rejects the tool_search tool type
      - upstream rejects defer_loading
      - response protocol explicitly reports unsupported tool search
    required_action_after_hard_failure: >-
      Record unsupported for the exact route, rebuild Codex model metadata with
      supports_search_tool=false, and make Codex construct a new request so MCP
      schemas are exposed directly. Retrying the already-built deferred request
      is insufficient.
    current_architecture_restart_required: true
    reason: >-
      The running Codex process owns the static model catalog and decides MCP
      exposure before the request reaches the Ciel router. Router-side state
      cannot retroactively add direct MCP definitions to that request.
    unsafe_failure_signals:
      - model returns ordinary text without calling tool_search
      - model returns an empty or reasoning-only turn
      - request times out
      - no MCP tool was needed for the task
    conclusion: >-
      Optimistic true may be combined with hard-failure fallback, but it cannot
      be the only detector. Silent semantic non-use is ambiguous and must not be
      automatically classified unsupported.

  always_true_risk_evidence:
    assumption_rejected: >-
      An unsupported model does not harmlessly ignore Tool Search while keeping
      direct MCP tools. Codex chooses deferred versus direct exposure before the
      request reaches the model.
    official_behavior: >-
      Deferred MCP exposes only the server or namespace description initially;
      individual tool definitions are loaded only through Tool Search.
    mia_observation:
      session: 01a03cf6-4f1d-76b1-8d25-94c658c572e3
      evidence:
        - AI-Net checkin and other direct MCP functions were absent from the model-visible tool list.
        - The model attempted resources/read for uri checkin instead.
        - AI-Net returned MCP -32601 Method not found.
        - Mia created a direct JSON-RPC helper because the direct MCP calls were unavailable.
      conclusion: >-
        Always-true without a verified Tool Search path can remove functional
        MCP access rather than merely add an unused capability.
    security_note: >-
      The inspected remote transcript contains an AI-Net API key in plaintext.
      The value is intentionally omitted from this journal and should be treated
      as exposed.

  prompt_guided_self_recovery:
    prompt_only_sufficient: false
    confirmed_limit: >-
      A system prompt can instruct a capable model to call tool_search, but it
      cannot add a missing tool schema, implement unsupported wire item types,
      or mutate the client-side Codex ModelInfo that selected deferred exposure.
    useful_prompt_behavior:
      - Use tool_search before list_mcp_resources or list_mcp_resource_templates when MCP functions are needed.
      - Never treat MCP resources APIs as substitutes for MCP tool discovery.
      - If tool_search is absent, rejected, or cannot load a required tool, emit a bounded structured recovery request rather than inventing a workaround.
    required_recovery_surface: >-
      Provide a Ciel recovery function or router-recognized structured marker
      that is always direct and never deferred with MCP tools. The router can
      then persist direct mode for the exact route and perform one controlled
      resume/retry using supports_search_tool=false.
    reliability_limit: >-
      A prose-only marker remains model-dependent and may be omitted or emitted
      incorrectly. A forced compatibility probe or an always-direct typed
      recovery function is stronger evidence and should bound retries to one.

  official_references:
    codex_spec_plan: >-
      https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/ff29a44391deccde0aba0f8390337d7f3c319ea4/codex-rs/core/src/tools/spec_plan.rs
    codex_model_fallback: >-
      https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/ff29a44391deccde0aba0f8390337d7f3c319ea4/codex-rs/models-manager/src/model_info.rs
    openai_gpt_5_4_nano: >-
      https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5.4-nano
    capability_distinction: >-
      The official GPT-5.4 nano model page lists MCP as supported and Tool
      search as not supported, proving these are distinct capabilities.

  verification:
    type: read_only_source_log_and_catalog_inspection
    cli_evidence_collected: true
    ui_screenshot_required: false
    status: research_complete_no_fix_applied
